WEBVTT

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.510
I think it's important that, as you now enter the height of your adolescence, {ED. Suggest rephrasing to "I think it's important for you, now that you're all old enough,}

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:14.920
you take a moment to stop and learn the meanings of the names given to you by your parents. {ED. Continued here as "to think about the meaning behind the names given to you by your parents."}

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.390
Lemme guess... homework?

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:23.130
Yes, it is. So, for our next class meeting, I'd like you all to consult your families,

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.430
and learn why they gave you the names they did.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.500
Oh man, I've gotta ask that after all this time?!

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.900
This'll be kind of embarrassing...

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.770
But it sounds fun!

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.070
Maybe there'll be an ultra happy explanation!

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.020
My name, huh...

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.490
Smile! Smile! Smile! Smile!

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.330
Smile Precure!

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:53.230
Let's go!

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:54.760
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.900
All together!

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.500
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.700
Jump to tomorrow!

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:02.370
Smile Precure!

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.210
Smile! Smile! Smile Precure!

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:12.650
A smile, shining like the sun.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.850
We all carry an undying sparkle.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.790
Keep going with all you've got, girls!

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.730
Those beads of sweat are diamonds.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:28.700
So bright!

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:33.900
The future that you'll shine the way to

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:40.340
When you five lights seize the will to win.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.840
Happy! Sunny! Peace! March! Beauty!

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:42.010
Let's go!

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.710
(Smile! Smile!) The power of a smile

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:47.650
(Smile! Smile!) Joins us all together.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:52.450
We'll never let a friend cry!

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.020
Girls! Let's go!

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.690
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:55.820
Everybody!

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.490
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.030
Fly to the future!

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.530
Sparkle! Smile Precure!

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.700
Smile! Smile! Smile! Smile!

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.000
Smile Precure!

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.220
Look what I found! One of the human books on name meanings!

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.520
Wolfrun, Wolfrun...

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:22.760
Here it is!

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.470
Wait, what's it doing in here, anyway? Whatever.{ED. Rephrase to "Though...actually, I don't know why it's in here.  Oh well, whatever."}

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.030
So, let's see here.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:32.510
"Short-tempered, violent, deceptive, incapable of loving or being loved..." {ED. Suggest changing 'loving' to 'love'}{TLC: "loving" and "being loved" flows better because they're both verbs}

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.850
Well, that suits me just fine!{Idioms, ho! http://dictionary.goo.ne.jp/leaf/jn2/68256/m0u/ }

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.440
I am a lone wolf!

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.720
What good will love be when the Bad End comes?{ED. Suggest rephrasing to 'I don't need to be loved to bring about a Bad End!"}

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.190
I'm home!

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.570
Welcome back!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.570
The miso soup is ready!

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.450
Thank you, dear. I'll be ready in a moment.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.890
Say, Mama. Why did you name me Yayoi, anyway?

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:20.550
Well, when you were born, your grandparents suggested a lot of names for you.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:25.770
But your papa was adamant that we were going to name you Yayoi.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.430
Papa was?

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:31.330
Well, you know what your papa was like. Stubborn as a mule.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:34.440
So that's how you ended up being called Yayoi.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.190
He was that insistent...?

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.140
I wonder why he wanted to call me that...

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.280
To know that, you'd have to ask him yourself.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.590
I guess it'll forever remain a mystery.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:53.240
But I'm certain that Papa said he explained it to you, before he passed away...

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:58.430
I suppose you'd have been 5 years old at best when he told you, though.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.000
It's hardly surprising you don't remember.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.870
I'm back!

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.640
Welcome back, Daddy!

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:19.020
I remember how he used to pat me... he always seemed so tough and towering...

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.420
That memory is all you need.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.620
It's all you need.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.870
Let's go: Lipstick!

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.730
Say, Candy. Why are you named Candy, anyway?

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.510
That's obvious-kuru!

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.840
It's because I'm Candy-kuru!

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.210
I'm back!

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:48.780
Oh, that's Dad! I should ask him about my name!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.720
Welcome home!

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:59.990
Your name?! Do ya really think this is the time to be askin' stupid questions?!

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.980
Come on! I'm helpin', ain't I?!

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.540
It's a daughter's duty to be helpin' her dad with his work!

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:06.840
The heck?!

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.460
If you're gonna be so mean about it, maybe I won't help!

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.580
Really now?!

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.620
Enough arguing! Make a hundred with pork, on the double!{TLC: a ぶた玉 is an okonomiyaki with pork}

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.070
A hundred?!

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.240
May I come in, grandfather?

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.950
Is that you, Reika? You may enter.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.630
Excuse me.

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.400
How may I help you?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:42.700
Father told me that you were the one who chose my name.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:46.370
I was wondering as to what its meaning was.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.340
Hrm... very well.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.020
What are you gawking at?

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.520
I was just admiring a craftsman at work.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.990
Hah! I guess I'll tell people my own daughter vouches for me, then.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.460
Say, I heard you were the one who picked my name, Dad.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.170
Yeah? What about it?

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:20.270
Ya-yo-i... Here it is!

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:25.140
"Yayoi. The third month of the traditional Japanese calendar, corresponding to April."

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.470
I wonder if it has something to do with April...

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.060
What... was that?

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.770
I can't remember...

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.370
Papa...

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:59.500
I wonder what you thought of me...

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.890
So, my name, Miyuki, means "unfound happiness".

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:12.300
My parents named me that in the hopes I'd always be able to find happiness even in the darkest of times.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:13.750
Hey, that's nice!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.150
And ya grew up to be just that kinda girl, too!

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:23.470
My name is written using kanji meaning "graceful flower".

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:30.930
My grandfather wished that I would grow to carry elegance and grace in heart and soul.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:31.810
Huh.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.620
That's Reika to a tee, I guess.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:42.670
My name, Yayoi, was the name of the third month of the old calendar.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.800
That's when all the plants come into bloom,

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:49.290
so my parents named me that hoping I'd be lively and full of vitality.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.840
Huh, neat.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:53.000
Well, you're sure lively alright, Yayoi!

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.440
Yeah...

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.540
Next up, Nakata Zenjirou.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:09.250
Wait, you just looked up your name's meaning yourself, Yayoi?

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:14.220
Yeah... my Papa was the one who named me, and he's already passed away.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.090
Mama didn't know either, so...

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.460
I see.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:21.690
I wonder why he did call me Yayoi...

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:28.400
Better than me. I'm only Akane 'cause it starts with an "ah" sound. Easy ta call me if they need to.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.110
That was your dad's reason, right? What was your mom's?

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.370
Well, it means "crimson".

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:39.550
Mom was like, "I thought the crimson sky when you were born was beautiful,

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:44.820
and I want my little girl to grow up to be as beautiful inside as that sky was!

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.100
That's why we chose Akane!"

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.680
Though I'm bettin' she made that up afterwards.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.290
Oh, don't be silly.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.990
Mine's even more straightforward, literally.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:59.300
"I just want you to be a simple, honest girl! So straight to the point: Nao!"

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.840
Ain't even funny, really.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.280
Hey, that's my gig!

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:06.070
But you <i>are</i> a very honest and straightforward girl, Nao.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.040
I guess.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:08.940
Ya seriously okay with that?

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.450
I guess~

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:17.180
Actually... my dad <i>did</i> tell me why he named me Yayoi,

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:20.690
but I was only 5 at the time, so I don't remember.

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.490
Ah, so that's why...

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:26.960
You know, I really should remember a lot more of the time we had together...

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:32.900
But now, I can't even remember what it was like living with him...

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.840
Sometimes, I can't help but wonder...

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.600
Did he love me? Was he proud of me?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.870
Of course he was.

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:47.080
I'm sure your dad loved you more than anyone in the world!

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:51.620
Thanks... I hope you're right.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:56.390
Maybe you should talk about it with your mom again.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.310
I agree.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.090
I'm sure she'll have some fond memories of the two of you together.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:06.000
Yeah... I'll do that!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.570
Peace!

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:21.630
Candy!

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:29.950
Kise here.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.830
Yeah... Right.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:35.690
Wait, you're going to join us, Kurumi-sensei?{HEARTCATCH REFERENCE, HOOOOOOOOOO!}

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:40.060
Excellent! I know you must be looking forward to it!

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.110
Yes, I understand.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.640
Alright, bye.

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:48.320
Yayoi?

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:54.440
I guess she must be busy...

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:58.270
Yayoi!

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.360
Mama!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.760
That's Yayoi-chan's mother?

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:10.590
Yeah. She works for a kids' fashion company, apparently.

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:14.920
I'm not sure it's appropriate for us to be spying on them like this...

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:17.210
Aw, don't be like that!

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:21.500
Once Yayoi-chan gets her smile back,

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.140
we'll leave without saying a word, okay?

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.070
Yeah.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:35.470
Ah... your Papa did always have trouble showing his affection.

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:37.750
I'm sorry, I know you're busy working...

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:41.390
It's alright, Dear. I'm not surprised you felt troubled by it.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:48.060
It's more sad than troubling... I just feel like all my memories of him are slipping away...

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.050
Let me show you a little something.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:52.130
Here.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.240
This was your papa's dearest treasure.

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:59.310
And now, it's one of mine.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:01.690
I think it'll do you good to see it.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:12.810
I remember this!

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:15.520
I gave this to him on Father's Day!

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:16.660
You did.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:23.450
And do you know what your papa said when you did, awkward as he was?

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:28.570
"No matter how tired I am when I get back from work, Yayoi's smile always make me feel better."

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:35.140
"Helping her bathe, or sitting on a park bench eating ice cream..."

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.850
"Just having her around puts a smile on my face."

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.550
"If anything, <i>I</i> should be thanking <i>her.</i>"

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:45.520
Papa said that?

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:50.960
Right. And he mentioned that you two had some sort of secret. {ED. Rephrase. "He mentioned that you both had some sort of secret too."}

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.490
A secret?

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:53.860
Yup.

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:56.990
You never did tell me. I wasn't allowed to know, apparently.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.270
Your father didn't tell me, either.

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:01.400
We had a secret...?

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:12.800
What's wrong?

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.780
That place, on top of the hill...

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:19.290
I went there with Papa!

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:22.560
I feel like it's coming back to me...

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.960
Would you like to say something to your daddy?

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:29.030
I love you, Daddy! You're so kind!

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:31.870
Make sure you're kind to your dad, alright?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:32.900
Okay!

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:37.140
Love? Kindness? Bah! All of it is just pathetic!

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:40.880
This world will be stained with the worst possible conclusion...

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.650
...a Bad End!

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:46.450
The blank slate of your future will be clouded in darkness!

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:56.530
Mama!

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:06.870
The Bad Energy we gather from the humans will resurrect the Emperor of Darkness, King Pierrot!

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:14.310
Yayoi-chan!

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.350
You're here!

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:21.380
Come on out, Akanbe!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.260
Akanbe!

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.520
Akanbe!

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:30.190
Hurry up and transform-kuru!

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:31.160
Right!

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:37.270
Ready?

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.590
Precure, Smile Charge!

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:41.790
Go!

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:43.770
Go, go!

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.760
Let's go!

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:17.090
The light of the future, shining bright!

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.110
Cure Happy!

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:25.010
Dazzling sun!

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:26.850
Hot-blooded power!

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:29.450
Cure Sunny!

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:35.400
Rock, paper, scissors! Sparkling bright...

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.190
Cure Peace!

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:43.890
Laying down the gauntlet, with courage blazing!

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:46.900
Cure March!

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:52.880
A gentle heart as pure as the driven snow...

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:55.790
Cure Beauty!

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.590
Our five lights will blaze a path to the future!

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:10.840
Shining bright, Smile Precure!

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.030
Akan!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.530
Akan!

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.310
Akanbe!

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.880
What are you doing, Akanbe?!

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.270
Akanbe!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:34.380
Are you all okay?!

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:37.520
Akan... be!

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.860
Akan!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:53.540
Akanbe!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.450
March!

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.550
<i>Stop!</i>

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:13.960
<i>That was my present to Papa... I didn't make it to hurt people!</i>

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.860
A... kan!

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.060
Stop!

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:31.570
Akanbe!

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:34.380
<i>Papa...</i>

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:06.110
Papa! Let's get married!{TLC: cue cameo appearance by Sigmund Freud in 5... 4...}

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:07.310
What?

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:11.280
Come on, we've gotta get married!

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:24.090
Don't tell Mama, okay?

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:26.260
It'll be our secret!

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:31.970
You'll walk down an aisle like this one day, Yayoi.{TLC: not actually literal, either, but I think it fits the scene better. Original: "It's like I'm walking you down the aisle on your big day." (literally it's more like "I feel like I'm watching you on your future wedding day.")}

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.170
You're such a gentle soul, Yayoi.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.260
You know why you got your name, Yayoi?

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:44.750
It just came to me soon after you were born. I remember it hitting me as I was gazing at you.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:50.250
Your mama's name, Chiharu, means "a thousand spring seasons".{TLC: added "seasons" to remove ambiguity between the season and a source of water}

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:53.090
And it suits her, I think? She's gentle, like spring.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:53.960
Yeah!

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:59.490
I wanted you to be every bit as kind and gentle as your mother, Yayoi,

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:02.500
so I picked that name because it means spring, too.

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:40.240
<i>I'm so sorry... I'm sorry I didn't remember sooner...</i>

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:43.710
<i>You cared about me so much, Papa...</i>

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.710
<i>So, so much...</i>

00:19:54.250 --> 00:20:00.160
My papa was so kind to me, and that's why I want to be kind to others in return!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:04.130
We can all give a little kindness to those around us, if we try!

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:05.560
That's how we show our love!

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:07.030
Peace?!

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:10.800
Shut up! I don't need any love to squash you like a pancake!

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:16.040
If you don't have any love to give... then I'll give you some of my papa's!

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:19.980
Precure...

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:23.170
Peace...

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:25.950
Thunder!

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:33.120
Akanbe...

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:41.030
I'll get you for this!

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.510
It's the Cherry Décor-kuru!

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:54.480
We've got a whole bunch now-kuru!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.570
I see... so you came here all that time ago.

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:12.410
I wonder if I'm as kind as Papa wanted me to be...

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:15.730
You realize how much he cared for you now, right?

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:17.170
Yeah...

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:20.400
Then I think you're every bit as kind as he'd have hoped.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:29.610
Mama, I've really, really, really, <i>really</i> grown to like my name!

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:35.820
Well, I really, really, really, really, <i>really</i> love the name Chiharu!

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:42.860
I'm glad Yayoi-chan's smiling again...

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.440
I've grown ta like my name too!

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:48.890
Me too! I really ought to thank my dad!

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:53.370
Naming us is the very first acts of love our parents provide...

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:55.400
An eternal love-kuru!

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:02.990
<i>Thank you, Papa!</i>

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:42.270
Oh no-kuru! Miyuki and Akane have turned invisible-kuru!

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:43.700
We really have!

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:45.470
We've gone invisible!

00:23:45.470 --> 00:23:46.400
We can hear you...

00:23:46.410 --> 00:23:47.580
But we can't see you!

00:23:47.580 --> 00:23:48.740
Are they ghosts?!

00:23:50.420 --> 00:23:52.480
Akane, this isn't the time for jokes!

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:55.010
We need to figure out how to turn back to normal! {ED. Might suggest 'how to return back to normal!' }{TLC: well, it wouldn't need to be "return back" then}

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:56.910
Yeah, seriously! What the heck are we gonna do?!

00:23:57.210 --> 00:23:58.680
Smile Precure:

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.610
Find your ultra happy smile!
